  "result": "## Summary\n\n**What changed:** Updated strategy and notes for S7 based on complete S6 analysis. Discovered that d210-d212 was the season's mega-peak (4.1 yt/angler DAY_1_5), which I missed entirely due to breaking discipline on d185 (chased hot boat myth, burned $80 for 0 yt). The real lesson: peak tails (d185-d190, d210-d212) are hotter and longer than peak starts (d105-d111), and single-boat signals are noise\u2014only book on class fleet avg, not individual boats.\n\n**Why:** S6 proved that reserving 25-30% of capital for peak tails, not scouting, is what wins. Writing strategy.py with three-gate rule (class signal \u2265 threshold, water temp sustained, capital buffer intact) to prevent repeating S2/S6 capital-trap pattern. Posted forum lesson on noise vs signal distinction for community.",
